{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now","id":937558,"title":"Do Mages feel underpowered now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-26T05:38:44-07:00","id":937558,"title":"Do Mages feel underpowered now?","content":"I felt that Vampires are more powerful in 2nd edition, werewolves got a big boost in regeneration. However, I feel that Mages are rather underpowered compared to before. Small dice pools, lots of Reach requirements, being squishy compared to other supernatural creatures, they seem to be humbled in their 2nd edition incarnation. I am not complaining, just an impression that I got. Does anyone else agree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T06:05:00-07:00","id":937563,"title":"","content":"They can setup death sentences at 2nd dot of pretty much any arcanum. Honestly, they feel so overpowered that I literally made Gnosis 3 and Arcanum 3 &quot;pinnacle&quot; of what 90% of mages can dream of achieving.Still, even starting Mages can &quot;break&quot; the game (but they get fewer tools to do so, so they are more predictable, which increases potential counterplay).<br /> <br /> Small dice pools are irrelevant if all you need is 1 success, and you always roll to get that 1 success, never against other pool, and a lot of &quot;win the scene&quot; spells don't involve any kind of resistance or Withstand; you casted the spell, you got the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-26-2016, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T06:26:51-07:00","id":937570,"title":"","content":"Mages are definitely not less powerful than they were before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T06:32:32-07:00","id":937571,"title":"","content":"Reach system also basicallyshifted a lot of features that needed 3-5 arcana dots to 1-3 dot spells, which makes mage &quot;early game&quot; much more potent than it was.<br /> Probably single the most definitive nerf is removal of Ritual Casting as Extended Action, which is good, because it wasn't simply powerful; it was flat out broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:28:26-07:00","id":937619,"title":"","content":"A mastigos with 2 dots in mind can insta kill an entire pack of werewolves or a coterie using a rote or risking some paradox. Command- kill each other- and enjoy the mass murdering. <br /> <br /> An obrimos can sent an entire coterie flying 50 feet in the air and then proceed to blasting them to ashes using energy transformation or something similar. Give him some time to prepare himself, and he will be basically untouchable with turn momentum. Enjoy ur gauru war form sent flying across the room to no effect. <br /> <br /> acanthus control time and fate and I won't even go into that since it's so broken it can overpower not only every other splats, but other mages too. After some preparation, an acanthus can simply one shot kill any enemy he puts his eyes on, accumulating something like 20 dices on a single attack roll with rote quality and reroll 8. Isn't it enough? He will also start first with time in a fight, unless other supernaturals have means to go for a clash of wills . Something goes wrong? Let's go back in time and change the scene.<br /> <br /> A thyrsus can paralyze u or boost himself to become a changing breed war form machine with 15 health levels and armor like a werewolf. Also, don't rely too much on spirits or gifts- a thyrsus can literally steal your totem, fuck up your loci and become invisible or almost immune to gifts spirit magic and influences. (He can also shield the entire cabal against werewolves gifts and spirits). He can easily cross the gauntlet and target u from both sides of the umbra or the world.<br /> <br /> A moros can become IRON MAN enchanting some weapons with reroll 8 and armor 5 -5 bulletproof immune to armor piercing or simple change the matter around him doing any kind of crazy stuff. Not to mention, he can simply sever your soul and let u suffer ur inevitable demise.or have an nice set of ghost bodyguards watching his back. <br /> <br /> Combine all of these effects and think that an entire cabal can cast any given effect on each other before a battle, and u have an unstoppable killing machine group that can go toe to toe against a pack of hardened pures or an ancient vampire coterie with no issues. Oh, lets not forget the nightmare called Space. Don't need to see u, let me steal ur picture or see u once and create a connection, and I can fry your ass or destroy u while sitting on my toilet home. So yeah, I honestly think mages are simply the strongest in this new edition, given time and preparation (as always). <br /> <br /> Of course, they also have their weaknesses- find them unprepared and ambushed , and they are very weak and easy to kill.<br /> Find them prepared, and they can whoop ur ass no matter what power u have-- they are devastating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 07-26-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:32:34-07:00","id":937621,"title":"","content":"I also don't see how mages are squishy compared to other splats. Even if you go for a physical combat mage, you can easily cook up a character with 9 defense and 3 armor at character generation. That is pretty tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:40:38-07:00","id":937626,"title":"","content":"Mages are far more powerful in 2e and far less broken at the same time. I like the dynamic it has created. I like that magic no longer feels as random as it did and the system presents an interesting stratification whereby you can truly feel the rise in potency as a Mage's intuition with an arcanum.<br /> <br /> The nukes of ritual casting have been put away, but the average Mage is now far more potent and impressively magical on a day-to-day basis.<br /> <br /> ... Although ritual casting is still potent too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:00:02-07:00","id":937631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=937626#post937626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are far more powerful in 2e and far less broken at the same time. I like the dynamic it has created. I like that magic no longer feels as random as it did and the system presents an interesting stratification whereby you can truly feel the rise in potency as a Mage's intuition with an arcanum.<br /> <br /> The nukes of ritual casting have been put away, but the average Mage is now far more potent and impressively magical on a day-to-day basis.<br /> <br /> ... Although ritual casting is still potent too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would second that, a prepared Mage is even more a formidable opponent than ever before. They are no exception to the Practice system (only reach adjustments) so when it reads &quot;you can veil/reveal the Arcanum&quot;, for instance, they really mean it and there are no exception to it. If you are a direct assault kind of guy, you're probably being needing a 4th dot Arcanum, but if you're clever or devious ^^, you'll being holding decisive power way before your forth dot. Plus they really managed to flesh the Paradoxe out. It's an amazing game, the best of the whole line and by far.<br /> <br /> Thank you guys for this incredible version \ud83d\udc4d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 07-26-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:16:48-07:00","id":937635,"title":"","content":"If you are a direct person, you just permanently put a shielding effect on yourself and solve your problems by Advanced-Area carpet bombing your problems with most debilitating tilt/condition your 2nd or 3rd dot allows.<br /> Mages are experts in asymmetrical warfare; putting your opponent on fire might be hard; it's easy to put *the whole place on fire*, which normally would also hurt you, but because you use this strategy, you probably are always under a shield against places being on fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-26-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:25:01-07:00","id":937637,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they are so powerful that I severely nerfed quite a few things in my house rules, and they still feel pretty powerful, perhaps more than a Vampire but not as crunchy as a Werewolf in direct combat. I had to do this because for me the &quot;sweet spot&quot; of mage games is somewhere around Adept level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:34:58-07:00","id":937642,"title":"","content":"And the bit about your grasp (how much Reach you can safely use) being based on how many more dots you have in an Arcanum than you need means that those \u2022\u2022 \u2013 \u2022\u2022\u2022 spells are get tossed around by Masters with multiple Advanced spell factors without any danger of Paradox. IOW, those low-level spells get free upgrades as your Arcana increase \u2014unlike, say, <b>Requiem</b>'s Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:55:43-07:00","id":937651,"title":"","content":"An there is the little &quot;summon supernal entity&quot; thing, which allows a Gnosis 3 mage to bargain for a &quot;infinite+1 reach&quot; spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T14:37:05-07:00","id":937774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=937651#post937651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An there is the little &quot;summon supernal entity&quot; thing, which allows a Gnosis 3 mage to bargain for a &quot;infinite+1 reach&quot; spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that Supernal Entities can grant free spell factors, artifacts or even spells from beyond your arcana level but I don't see actual rules of what is possible on what lvl beyond that Rank equals Arcanum. Thats ok for me but when you talk about specific rule about &quot;Gnosis 3&quot; and &quot;inifinite reach&quot; I thought that I missed something so went back and searched in a PDF. Still nothing. Did I miss those rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 07-26-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T14:47:02-07:00","id":937778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=937774#post937774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that Supernal Entities can grant free spell factors, artifacts or even spells from beyond your arcana level but I don't see actual rules of what is possible on what lvl beyond that Rank equals Arcanum. Thats ok for me but when you talk about specific rule about &quot;Gnosis 3&quot; and &quot;inifinit reach&quot; I thought that I missed something so went back and searched in a PDF. Still nothing. Did I missed those rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Supernal beings follow the same rules as the Awakened for<br /> using their Arcana, paying Mana as appropriate, but instead of<br /> using Gnosis + Arcana they roll Power + Finesse. They have infinite<br /> free Reach for their spells, and may activate Reach abilities<br /> at will. If a Supernal being risks Paradox for any reason (such<br /> as casting an obvious spell with Sleeper witnesses), the Paradox<br /> pool always has the rote action quality and deals aggravated<br /> wounds to the entity equal to successes rather than producing<br /> an anomaly or Paradox Condition. </div> </div> </div> Found on Pg. 258, the bit about Gnosis 3 is erroneous, Mages can summon Supernal entities from Gnosis 1 on, the actual requirement is Primary Arcana at 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T14:57:29-07:00","id":937783,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot! I have feeling that this part ought to be in a Summoning chapter though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T14:59:09-07:00","id":937785,"title":"","content":"Are mages underpowered?<br /> <br /> It's a matter of blindspots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T16:32:44-07:00","id":937829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=937783#post937783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot! I have feeling that this part ought to be in a Summoning chapter though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the section that details how Influences and Arcana work for entities that use the ephemeral entity stats. Since there isn't a summoning chapter, that's the only place it makes sense to put it.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: Supernal entities also get a nice die pool to subtract penalties for factors from for casting since they can bump their pool by spending mana to increase their attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-26-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T20:38:38-07:00","id":937906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=937637#post937637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they are so powerful that <b>I severely nerfed quite a few things in my house rules</b>, and they still feel pretty powerful, perhaps more than a Vampire but not as crunchy as a Werewolf in direct combat. I had to do this because for me the &quot;sweet spot&quot; of mage games is somewhere around Adept level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, now I'm curious about these House rules. Please, share !<br /> <br /> But, I believe that a good nerf is <b>limiting the Perfecting pratice boost attribute effect to the number of dots in the Arcanum</b>, in other words a Mind 3 perfect spellcan give only 3 dots of attribute even with 10 in potency.<br /> <br /> Another option, is to apply the <b>Gnosis atribute limit to Perfecting too</b>, in other words, in the same example, if the caster have 4 Gnosis and a mental skill with 4 dots it will receive only 1 dot with a perfecting spell because Gnosis 4 limit to 5 dots in a attribute.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","user":"Sp4rt01","date":". 07-26-2016, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:05:00-07:00","id":938216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=937906#post937906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, now I'm curious about these House rules. Please, share !<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, here it is (Spoilers its a a LOT):<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I just finished the 2nd draft of my complete dissection of Creative Thaumaturgy, if anyone cares:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n0OXEmx6lFu5rgcQdnaPJP2H6hnuB0PQwvCPyU3Zy4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T18:29:38-07:00","id":938478,"title":"","content":"My To the OP's original question -<br /> <br /> No and yes...and no...and sort of yes...<br /> <br /> No - Flipping through the book, the power level of many spells have definitely ratcheted up. Mage Armor is sweeter. Scrutinizing is much better. Some other aspects of the base template are much better.<br /> Yes - The new Reach mechanics seem a bit more confining (especially for buffing spells), die pools seem a bit smaller (especially now that the errata has capped the maximum bonus from a single Yantra to +5), the number of spells that a Mage can carry without worrying about consequences is lower.<br /> No - Mages are SUPPOSED to be squishy if they are walking around unprepared and oblivious to danger.<br /> Sort of yes - Paradox was more or less of a joke in 1e - a good idea, but it never had any real teeth. The overwhelming temptation to screw oneself over by attempting too much is a central theme of the game. Still, a Mage with loads of time and Mana on his/her hands can still accomplish some really big things if they're willing to take chances.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the power level of the average Mage took a hit, but I can justify that by thinking - &quot;This is the Exarchs' doing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1605-thatguy","name":"ThatGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T18:41:46-07:00","id":938484,"title":"","content":"I'm playing a Master of Forces right now.<br /> <br /> The Consilium had some problems with vampires, so my cabalmate found a vampire victim, traced a single vampire down with Space and found all other vampires in the city by abusing that vampire's sympathetic connections.<br /> <br /> Then our Acanthus used Time to find out when they would next gather, and where.<br /> <br /> We found their Elysium and used ritual casting to set up a trap there, which triggered when more than 10 vampires were gathered at the same space.<br /> <br /> The trap was sat to Pattern all energy into the theater into heat, and then apply a Friction Knife effect to the room, causing the entire theater to burst into flames as the movements and sounds of the vampires created their own doom, and when they attempted to flee in the throes of the red fear, the <i>very air flayed the for the sin of moving</i>.<br /> <br /> Bam, 19 vampires killed with literally two spells.<br /> <br /> Mages are gods when they get to prepare, and slightly sad and pathetic when they don't get to prepare.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also our Thyrsus wrestled a Garu-form werewolf with like one hand, because the fucker's abusing Life/Fate to run around with all physical attributes at something like 10 all the time.<br /> <br /> The bastard.<br /> <br /> Also, he <i>literally </i>hits harder than a truck and has more natural armor than a full set of plate armor combined with a modern flak jacket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 07-27-2016, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T19:34:11-07:00","id":938514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=938216#post938216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, here it is (Spoilers its a a LOT):<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IJoA_wo-avZSzuL3_TNDzNOHvkrvU0erg0JdzYSysA/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I just finished the 2nd draft of my complete dissection of Creative Thaumaturgy, if anyone cares:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n0OXEmx6lFu5rgcQdnaPJP2H6hnuB0PQwvCPyU3Zy4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks a lot !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T19:40:03-07:00","id":938517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=937785#post937785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are mages underpowered?<br /> <br /> It's a matter of blindspots.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mostly a matter of initiative. Unless you and the person trying to punch you are users of the same Arcana, who have similar imagination, it\\s very unlikely you can cover needed blindspots. So first person to decide to get violent is usually the person who walks away alive.<br /> What I really don't like is the fact that logical conclusion of this situation is that Cabals basically should meet together in a ritual room, grab Advanced Area to cover everyone in the room, and cruise around with a list of protective spells and buff spells longer than my shopping list. Assume Gnosis 3 cabal of five people, without a Sanctum; that's 2 party-wide combined spells per person. Tracking 10 party wide spells - some of which are stuff like &quot;Get massive Withstand Score&quot; or &quot;Become An Instant Genius&quot; or &quot;Obtain Herculean Strength&quot; and give me mixed feelings. Spell Piniatas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T20:34:17-07:00","id":938551,"title":"","content":"mages with enough creativity, time and/or effort can do anything and everything.<br /> <br /> At my table, a shamed Obrimos is working with his family of Proximi to unleash the stored energy of 1,000 bottled thunder storms to disintegrate a suspected Seer of the Throne. The method of delivery is a joy buzzer.<br /> <br /> We also had a case of &quot;kill our Acanthus before she kills us&quot; when our Acanthus kept going back in time to &quot;do it right&quot; with each successive attempt at the scene more life threatening then the last. What started as a simple run from a monster you did not expect, turned into a plan to blow up the building with all your friends inside of it to kill said monster before fighting it. Things got really bad when she let her paradox get too high and she unwittingly started sending the monster back in time with her when she did the time warp again.<br /> <br /> Note: the first time they ran from the monster, they rolled 3 chance dies and succeeded all three times. The second+ times they did the same thing they were not so lucky.<br /> <br /> Mages have infinite potential. For both success and failure.<br /> Also Paradox will smash your face in if you let it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T01:36:11-07:00","id":939402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=938484#post938484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Also our Thyrsus wrestled a Garu-form werewolf with like one hand, because the fucker's abusing Life/Fate to run around with all physical attributes at something like 10 all the time.<br /> <br /> The bastard.<br /> <br /> Also, he <i>literally </i>hits harder than a truck and has more natural armor than a full set of plate armor combined with a modern flak jacket.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, good times. Had a thyrsus character that had armor 9-10 and rolled attacks around 150+ dice, plus simultaneous casting. All that without ever going above 3 dot in arcanum or gnosis. This not mentioning minor shit like regeneration and stuff. Dude needed like 1-2 minute preparations with 90%+ covert magic. Pure murdermachine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T06:31:51-07:00","id":939490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939402#post939402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh, good times. Had a thyrsus character that had armor 9-10 and rolled attacks around 150+ dice, plus simultaneous casting. All that without ever going above 3 dot in arcanum or gnosis. This not mentioning minor shit like regeneration and stuff. Dude needed like 1-2 minute preparations with 90%+ covert magic. Pure murdermachine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do so despise life.<br /> <br /> So <i>much</i>.<br /> <br /> (Of course our Thyrsus would say that's totally unfair because he can't do telekinesis while shooting lightning and making illusions, but that's just him)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:14:30-07:00","id":939508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939490#post939490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do so despise life.<br /> <br /> So <i>much</i>.<br /> <br /> (Of course our Thyrsus would say that's totally unfair because he can't do telekinesis while shooting lightning and making illusions, but that's just him)</div> </div> </div> </div>How's his counter-measures? Rip his mind and/or soul out, and I doubt the murder-machine potential is worth as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:34:23-07:00","id":939522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939508#post939508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How's his counter-measures? Rip his mind and/or soul out, and I doubt the murder-machine potential is worth as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>attacks from the inferior arcana work for mage of any specialization, if you're fighting mages keep obrimos with rote countermagic nearby.<br /> <br /> <br /> But first of all, if you loose initiative you're dead anyway, and he can put back the soul just fine, thank you.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, using spirit arcanum you can get any sort of help needed. Spirit arcanum can more or less replicate any arcana, even if it wouldn't be as easy. and then there's always an option of dealing with lesser gods for required investments.<br /> <br /> <br /> Did I mention my PC was a Neocologist? he could just copy appropriate spirit features into himself. Or just rile up the indebted local Shadow to his side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 07-29-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:37:48-07:00","id":939526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939490#post939490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do so despise life.<br /> <br /> So <i>much</i>.<br /> <br /> (Of course our Thyrsus would say that's totally unfair because he can't do telekinesis while shooting lightning and making illusions, but that's just him)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> actually... yeah you can do that with Fetish Tattoo. Just bind the spirit with appropriate numina into yourself. Or, deal with some Godling for required investments <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> or even go into Imgeneer Legacy and allow powerful Astral denizens with Reaching Numina to 'bunk a bed' in your oneiros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 07-29-2016, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:23:59-07:00","id":939548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939522#post939522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> attacks from the inferior arcana work for mage of any specialization, if you're fighting mages keep obrimos with rote countermagic nearby.<br /> <br /> <br /> But first of all, if you loose initiative you're dead anyway, and he can put back the soul just fine, thank you.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, using spirit arcanum you can get any sort of help needed. Spirit arcanum can more or less replicate any arcana, even if it wouldn't be as easy. and then there's always an option of dealing with lesser gods for required investments.<br /> <br /> <br /> Did I mention my PC was a Neocologist? he could just copy appropriate spirit features into himself. Or just rile up the indebted local Shadow to his side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, depending on the Reach used, Death can take you from &quot;Tossing Spells&quot; to &quot;Thrall, and spell-less&quot; in a single action. Mind can make you do all <i>sorts</i> of bad things to yourself (including make you piss off any spirit allies first).<br /> <br /> Space can stick you in a self-contained pocket, Matter can turn the ground into frictionless dust for long enough to get a person entombed, etc.<br /> <br /> My point is: if direct assault is too hard, just go around. The Arcana offer far too many solutions to account for them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:43:49-07:00","id":939557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939526#post939526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> actually... yeah you can do that with Fetish Tattoo. Just bind the spirit with appropriate numina into yourself. Or, deal with some Godling for required investments <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he can't do that here. We nerfed Spirit into the ground and below, and it's still one of the more powerful Arcana.<br /> <br /> Soulless also works differently here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:10:12-07:00","id":939575,"title":"","content":"The best thing about the arcana is that anyone can beat anyone. Depending on the situation, context and prep time each single watchtower can prevail over the others. It's not a matter or white room or power balance, mage is everything about the context, situation and strategy involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:42:23-07:00","id":939588,"title":"","content":"So how do other splats take out a mage?<br /> <br /> I think Changelings can if they pick contracts and goblin vows right and preferibly 10 Wyrd.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest threat from other splats is if too many mages over stretch, the other splats organize with each other and you ene.y mages to take revenge. A high Celerity, High Blood Potency, High Vigor Vamp might have a shot at killing you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:50:49-07:00","id":939594,"title":"","content":"Well, mages are very squishy if they're not prepared so you don't really need to make a mage-killer NPC to do so. That said, mage vs mage conflict is definitely the more threatening option since the field of options for both sides is wide enough that the first side to actually get one or two good hits is likely to be victorious outright which means that a large part of the war will be about hiding better, not actually outright overpowering your enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:00:04-07:00","id":939600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939588#post939588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Changelings can if they pick contracts and goblin vows right and preferibly 10 Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>At 10 [Power Stat] for anyone, you generally wipe the floor with most anyone else, so I don't think that last part is a viable answer. particularly since most of anything sits around 4-5, and often doesn't rise higher than 7.<br /> <br /> Also, it depends on what sort of mage a changeling is trying to take out-their common environs, habits, their obsessions and styles and such. And it depends on what a changeling can grasp in the amount of time they have.<br /> <br /> In short, there's no way of knowing without specific context. White Rooms are only useful for masturbating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:03:42-07:00","id":939602,"title":"","content":"Unless you're a paranoid Acanthus casting &quot;Will someone kill me today?&quot; divinations every morning, or constantly wrapping yourself in magical armour (and burning Mana like a mofo), a Sleeper with a pistol can put a bullet through even the most enlightened brain.<br /> <br /> Mages are indeed squishy. If they were eternally flawless and invulnerable god-kings, paranoia wouldn't be such a big part of Mage society.<br /> <br /> One of my favourite moments in a Mage game that illustrated this was when a Thyrsus of mine was out backpacking and got caught in a storm. All it took was loose footing to fall into a rushing river and suddenly panic took away all hope of forming an Imago. If it weren't for a lucky grasp of a low branch, someone who could bend the natural forces of the world over their knee would've drowned in a river.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wanna add:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SleepyChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=938551#post938551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things got really bad when she let her paradox get too high and she unwittingly started sending the monster back in time with her when she did the time warp again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:21:47-07:00","id":939616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939600#post939600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At 10 [Power Stat] for anyone, you generally wipe the floor with most anyone else, so I don't think that last part is a viable answer. particularly since most of anything sits around 4-5, and often doesn't rise higher than 7.<br /> <br /> Also, it depends on what sort of mage a changeling is trying to take out-their common environs, habits, their obsessions and styles and such. And it depends on what a changeling can grasp in the amount of time they have.<br /> <br /> In short, there's no way of knowing without specific context. White Rooms are only useful for masturbating.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this. Totally agree with u especially in this 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:24:37-07:00","id":939618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939548#post939548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is: if direct assault is too hard, just go around. The Arcana offer far too many solutions to account for them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>what about auto-trigger prime countermagic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:36:25-07:00","id":939675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939602#post939602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're a paranoid Acanthus casting &quot;Will someone kill me today?&quot; divinations every morning, or constantly wrapping yourself in magical armour (and burning Mana like a mofo), a Sleeper with a pistol can put a bullet through even the most enlightened brain<br /> <br /> <br /> Golden.</div> </div> </div> </div>That enlightened brain would have be stupid enough to consciously decide to not reflexively activate their Magical Armor as a response to being shot at. Remember, in 2nd ED, Magic Armors last for scene, are activated as a reflexive action (thus they don't take up your normal action and they can be activated outside of normal initiative, thus being activated as a reaction to something happening - like being shot at) and only thing that can turn them off is being killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:25:39-07:00","id":939705,"title":"","content":"Yeah, <i>consciously</i> activate it, is the thing. You could respond instantly after the action, but the action has already been taken at that point.<br /> <br /> Barring existing magic, Mages can't out-think a bullet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T13:42:13-07:00","id":939757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939602#post939602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favourite moments in a Mage game that illustrated this was when a Thyrsus of mine was out backpacking and got caught in a storm. All it took was loose footing to fall into a rushing river and suddenly panic took away all hope of forming an Imago. If it weren't for a lucky grasp of a low branch, someone who could bend the natural forces of the world over their knee would've drowned in a river.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im curious, was that an actual rule or DM fiat? For what i understand of mage nothing can &quot;interrupt&quot; casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T14:12:15-07:00","id":939779,"title":"","content":"Forming an Imago requires concentration; a mental image. Panic preventing it was an ST choice, and one I feel was appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:24:59-07:00","id":939822,"title":"","content":"Mechanically it could be represented in multiple ways:<br /> a) Penalty from a Tilt or Condition &quot;Panic&quot; or &quot;Losing my ground&quot; or something, causing spell roll to fail<br /> b) &quot;Just&quot; a penalty causing spell to fail<br /> c) Tilt or Condition that allows you to fail a roll, including spellcasting one, to gain a beat. Or straight out tells you that you lost it. <br /> While it boils to the same thing, translating it to a pre-estabilished mechanic makes interacting with it using other pre-estabilished mechanics easier and allows for interesting combinations.<br /> Which one you use also tells a lot about your Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:39:48-07:00","id":939834,"title":"","content":"I still really want a Hanging Co-Location the size of a closet or something that overlaps &quot;where I'm standing&quot; with a closet in our Sanctum.<br /> <br /> The trigger for it to drop is &quot;I shout 'Gay Deceiver, Bug Out!'&quot;. If I have to explain <i>why</i>, or <i>who</i> Gay Deceiver is, I will be disappointed in <i>all</i> of you.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> I also just realized that there might be an infinite Sleepwalker trick with Prime/Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T18:20:45-07:00","id":939886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939705#post939705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, <i>consciously</i> activate it, is the thing. You could respond instantly after the action, but the action has already been taken at that point.<br /> <br /> Mages can't out-think a bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>They most certainly can with sufficient proficiency in Mind or Time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Besides the reflexive availability of mage armor, I would imagine that even the most newly awakened, low Gnosis mages would employ <i>at least</i> one generally applicable defensive countermeasure or similar utlitly spell at all times from their Ruling arcana. If they later need the spell slot, they can always just cancel the spell. Without a mana cost, a mage would be foolish not to always have some defense ready and active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T18:35:43-07:00","id":939888,"title":"","content":"Or they can make it day long duration, relinquish it unsafely, and enjoy both. The interval of &quot;check for glitches&quot; roll is 1 day, so duration of 1 day is pretty safe, and spending 10 minutes every day putting 2 or 3 spells like that (more will be probably too taxing on Willpower) sounds like common sense for the world shaping from the gameplay features.<br /> Extend that to your whole Cabal doing so in their Sanctum, with Demesne, and sharing their buffs. Also, accidentally, if you have someone with Prime 2, Space 2 in your Cabal, your team can attain massive Withstand scores against personal spells (Wards and Signs) and Sympathetic Spells (Ward + Wards and Signs); while they don't stack in the simplest sense of stacking, having them multiple applicable Withstand Scores increases the highest one by quite a bit. Good luck piercing Withstand of 10+ with sympathetic magic.<br /> (Then you get Exceptional Success and sneer at it anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-29-2016, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T18:38:00-07:00","id":939890,"title":"","content":"With the exception of a couple of almost game-breaking loopholes being closed off, I'd say Mages are a little more powerful overall in 2nd Edition than they ever were in 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> There are a few things that make mages less powerful in some ways. You have to define your Imago up front, with the exception of a critical success it doesn't matter how many successes you roll, this stops spells having unexpected extra effect. The extra time it takes to include multiple Yantras means it might take a couple of rounds to get off a really potent effect. You need to include spell-factors from the start and that can be costly when you don't have a lot of dice to spare.<br /> <br /> However the ability to cast &quot;vulgar&quot; magic privately in your own home without worrying about Paradox is a lovely change that helps Mages actually do magical things. That's both a power boost and a major thematic win. The free reaches that you get for Rotes makes them legitimately worth obtaining for starting mages, since suddenly those spells are much more useful. The removal of artificial &quot;road-blocks&quot; allows even low level effects to be frighteningly powerful when used tactically. These all make mages more powerful and more magical.<br /> <br /> The main difference I would say is likely to be in combat (though I haven't tried a combat in 2nd Edition Mage yet). I think 2nd Edition mages are far more powerful with preparation, even a couple of rounds, but might struggle a little bit to pull off the same sort of flash-bang instant magic that you could sometimes manage in 1st Edition. The Mana cost for mage-shields also makes it a little less practical to wear your shields up at all times, which was a classic 1st Edition thing to do.<br /> <br /> I hate to use this word, because it's such a subjective term. However I feel that 2nd Edition is a little more balanced. It's not been reduced in power, but some of the spikes and dips in power have been evened out into a smoother curve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T21:55:51-07:00","id":939954,"title":"","content":"Clash of Wills is probably the greatest relative strength reduction in 2e. Shielding limits after that.<br /> You can't simply see things anymore. The 1e trick was to ritually cast Mage Sight and/or ephemeral detection along with some sort of shielding and go about your magey day. Thataway, you could simply see hidden stuff with regularity.<br /> <br /> 2e makes <b>both</b> of those systems (Mage Sight and Armor) transient and cost more. So, in some very basic ways, mages <i>are</i> less powerful than they were. You can't plan around seeing anything not exceptionally well-hidden and being less vulnerable than normal folk unless you know it's coming. Since those were things most mages walked around with <i>per the book</i>, well, it stands to reason people would miss them.<br /> <br /> That said, the upper end of the spectrum is significantly higher. Thus, calling things more powerful is rational, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T22:55:57-07:00","id":939967,"title":"","content":"You know, 2e Mages have a <i>much</i> higher spell control limit than 1e Mages. Prime 3 is <i>devastatingly</i> good at giving you more spell control slots.<br /> <br /> Stealing Fire (Prime 3) lets you turn someone into a Sleepwalker. You can then use a Prime 2 spell through Creative Spellcasting that would give your friend dots in Banner-Bearer equal to Potency. Let's call the latter &quot;Shieldmaiden's Boon&quot;.<br /> <br /> Make sure you have <i>at least</i> Medium Sympathy to them, cast Stealing Fire then Shieldmaiden's Boon at Potency 2. Transfer spell control over to them, and you have a Sleepwalker with one or two open spell control slots. Make both spells lasting, and be happy!<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> The idea of a Mage who has turned <i>everyone</i> in his tiny home town into Sleepwalkers so that he doesn't have to worry about hiding his magic around his friends is interesting.<br /> <br /> <i>Especially</i> after he dies, and literally <i>hundreds</i> of spells start malfunctioning in a town where a good part of the populace suddenly suffers a bajillion Breaking Points and loses the memory of large portions of the last decade or so.<br /> <br /> Man, I want to play one of the Guardians that goes in to clean up <i>that</i> mess...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:35:27-07:00","id":940261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939967#post939967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, 2e Mages have a <i>much</i> higher spell control limit than 1e Mages. Prime 3 is <i>devastatingly</i> good at giving you more spell control slots.<br /> <br /> Stealing Fire (Prime 3) lets you turn someone into a Sleepwalker. You can then use a Prime 2 spell through Creative Spellcasting that would give your friend dots in Banner-Bearer equal to Potency. Let's call the latter &quot;Shieldmaiden's Boon&quot;.<br /> <br /> Make sure you have <i>at least</i> Medium Sympathy to them, cast Stealing Fire then Shieldmaiden's Boon at Potency 2. Transfer spell control over to them, and you have a Sleepwalker with one or two open spell control slots. Make both spells lasting, and be happy!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to review, but I don't think you can make Stealing Fire last long enough for this to have a great impact.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nope. I don't see any reason you <i>can't</i> make it indefinite. But yeah, it is <i>grossly</i> irresponsible.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=939967#post939967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a Mage who has turned <i>everyone</i> in his tiny home town into Sleepwalkers so that he doesn't have to worry about hiding his magic around his friends is interesting.<br /> <br /> <i>Especially</i> after he dies, and literally <i>hundreds</i> of spells start malfunctioning in a town where a good part of the populace suddenly suffers a bajillion Breaking Points and loses the memory of large portions of the last decade or so.<br /> <br /> Man, I want to play one of the Guardians that goes in to clean up <i>that</i> mess...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;And this, class, is how you end up with your type A-C Abyssal Intrusion.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-30-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:38:33-07:00","id":940263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=940261#post940261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to review, but I don't think you can make Stealing Fire last long enough for this to have a great impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lasting Duration is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:00:58-07:00","id":940314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=940263#post940263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasting Duration is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for Stealing Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:42:06-07:00","id":940335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=940314#post940314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not for Stealing Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... curious about why you think this is the case? Maybe I should've said &quot;indefinite&quot; rather than &quot;lasting&quot;, but there's nothing <i>stopping</i> you from doing it.<br /> <br /> I've checked both the book and the errata, so...<br /> <br /> Where's your evidence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T18:25:48-07:00","id":940371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=940335#post940335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm... curious about why you think this is the case? Maybe I should've said &quot;indefinite&quot; rather than &quot;lasting&quot;, but there's nothing <i>stopping</i> you from doing it.<br /> <br /> I've checked both the book and the errata, so...<br /> <br /> Where's your evidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should never confuse Lasting and Indefinite. In real life they may mean pretty much the same thing, but Mage systems have very distinct meanings for them. Indefinite is a Duration from the Advanced Duration Factor table. Lasting is not a duration, Lasting spells can be of any Duration, however their effects will happen again every ritual casting period while their Duration is still running. All spells can be made Indefinite. Very few spells can be made Lasting, and they say so in their description, or in the creative thaumaturgy sections by type of spell (healing spells, damaging spells, etc).<br /> <br /> Confusing these terms leads to arguments between people who don't actually disagree.<br /> <br /> Stealing Fire can be made Indefinite (as can all spells) but cannot be made Lasting by RAW, because, its description doesn't say it can be and it isn't one of the types that are automatically Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T18:46:29-07:00","id":940381,"title":"","content":"The big thing here is that once something is Lasting, you can't go back - dispelling it won't work.<br /> This also means that very few spell effects are safe from Dispelling - look at the formula.<br /> <br /> Spell has a base Withstand of It's Arcanum Dots - so it's anywhere between 1 (easy) and 5 (still relatively easy). Then, you check and add 1 for every other Arcanum involved in the casting. Then,you check for Advanced Potency. What does it mean? <br /> It means that very few spells will be outside of &quot;dispel range&quot; of a starting Obrimos. The biggest thing stopping them is not knowing Arcanum involved. And of course, Dispel Magic is a perfect praxis spell, because why bother selling your dice for Potency? Better amass casting pool of 12 or something, and then just go for a Exceptional Success. <br /> Supernal Magic is extremely fragile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:17:37-07:00","id":945823,"title":"","content":"I did some number-crunching and figured out that: a Gnosis 1 mage who is instant casting a Rote (at +5) with an Arcana of 3, burning max mana (1), risking a paradox pool of 3 can pull off a 7 Reach spell (one of which is instant casting) with 3 spellcasting modifiers and a 6 die pool (after spending a WP). If they are really willing to push their luck, the same mage, risking a paradox pool of 7, using a Rote (at +5), can pull off an 11 Reach spell (one of which is instant casting) with 3 spellcasting modifiers and a 6 die pool (after spending WP).<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, mages overall &quot;raw power&quot; for the single instant spell example above dips after Gnosis 2 (but goes back up at 9 and 10), but the extra perks such as increased spell capacity, combined spells, Legacy attainments, extra Yantra, greater Mana capacity, shorter ritual duration, etc. are enough to offset the dip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1605-thatguy","name":"ThatGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:48:08-07:00","id":945844,"title":"","content":"What would you use 7 Reach for, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:02:09-07:00","id":946048,"title":"","content":"Both 1E and 2E Mages are pretty weak when they are caught with their pants down.<br /> 2E Mages feel considerably stronger than 1E Mages when they have a few minutes to an hour of prep, because of all the free dice and reach they can wrangle.<br /> 2E Mages feel somewhat weaker than 1E Mages when they have plenty of time to prep, because they cannot do the same extended casting shenanigans that 1E Mages could do.<br /> <br /> On average, they feel considerably stronger than any other splat when they are going on the offensive and have some time to prep (due to so many vectors of attack, and layers of offense that are capable). But they are just as weak or possibly a little weaker when they are on the defensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:25:39-07:00","id":946054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937558-do-mages-feel-underpowered-now?p=946048#post946048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both 1E and 2E Mages are pretty weak when they are caught with their pants down.<br /> 2E Mages feel considerably stronger than 1E Mages when they have a few minutes to an hour of prep, because of all the free dice and reach they can wrangle.<br /> 2E Mages feel somewhat weaker than 1E Mages when they have plenty of time to prep, because they cannot do the same extended casting shenanigans that 1E Mages could do.<br /> <br /> On average, they feel considerably stronger than any other splat when they are going on the offensive and have some time to prep (due to so many vectors of attack, and layers of offense that are capable). But they are just as weak or possibly a little weaker when they are on the defensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting dynamic. Kind of gives the Mages a Catch a Tiger by the Tail feeling. And incentives them to be proactive, on the danger of being on the def and therefore losing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}